# The Flentrop of 1958, Adolphus Busch Hall: a stop
# for dacvoice (voices/README.md, "Stops"). The division's lines (n,
# frame, envelope, chiff) are the same in each of its stops, so they mix.
name Mixtuur IV
family Hoofdwerk
n 10
frame 8
start 18 dB
attack 0.012 s
peak 0 dB
decay 0 dB/s
sustain 0 dB
release 0.05 s
chiff 0.012 s 16 dB 2 16
# Hoofdwerk: four principal ranks, 1 1/3, 1, 2/3 and 1/2 foot at C, breaking
# back an octave at C4 (zone 3) and C5 (zone 4), the 1 foot at C5 and C6,
# so no rank passes a zone's top harmonic. Not the Flentrop's composition,
# which is not documented: a usual Dutch one.
harmonics 1 1.0  2 0.4  3 0.2  4 0.1
rank 6 1.0 break 4
rank 8 1.0 break 4 5
rank 12 0.8 break 3 4
rank 16 0.8 break 3 4
level 1 dB
# The voicing (voices/README.md, "The voicing"): the speech by the pipe's
# size, and Busch Hall, where the organ stands.
rise 10
room busch
# The celeste: a second read of the table at half the rate, 2 cents
# sharp, a rank a little off the unison.
celeste 2
